<!--
  A feed that dates its entries ahead of the clock.

  Three entries, fixed in time so a test can place `now` wherever the rule
  under examination needs it. Against a `now` of 2026-08-22T06:00:00Z:

    tomorrow   +14h  - a claim no clock supports
    soon        +3h  - inside any sane tolerance; embargoes and timezone
                       arithmetic produce this honestly
    settled      -1h  - the ordinary case

  Recency is a sort key, so a feed that dates its entries forward takes the top
  slot every single day and keeps it. That is the behaviour item 5 bounds.
-->
<rss version="2.0">
  <channel>
    <title>Example Forward Dating</title>
    <link>https://forward.example-press.net/</link>
    <description>A feed with an optimistic clock.</description>
